-- title:
--   Ramification of the X_H(M) dictionary equals stabiliser order
-- statement:
--   Fix $M \ge 1$ and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and let $\Gamma_H(M) =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) be the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained by pushing forward along the inclusion $\Gamma_0(M) \hookrightarrow \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ given by the lower-right entry modulo $M$. Let $F_0 =$ [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) be the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq F_0 \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ of $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma_H(M)$, and let $D$ be a complex place dictionary for the pair $(\Gamma_H(M), F_0)$: a datum consisting of a map $\mathrm{pt}$ from the upper half plane $\mathcal{H}$ to the places of the base change $\mathbb{C}\cdot F_0 \subseteq \mathbb{C}((q))$ (places being valuation subrings, proper, containing the base field and principal), a function $\mathrm{ramification} : \mathcal{H} \to \mathbb{N}$ with strictly positive values, invariance $\mathrm{pt}(\gamma \tau) = \mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_H(M)$, the requirement that $x$ lies in the valuation subring of $\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ exactly when the level-$\Gamma_H(M)$ realisation of $x$ has bounded modulus on a punctured neighbourhood of $\tau$, and the requirement that for $x \neq 0$ the meromorphic order at $\tau$ of that realisation equals $\mathrm{ramification}(\tau) \cdot \mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{pt}(\tau)}(x)$. Then for every $\tau \in \mathcal{H}$, $$2 \cdot \mathrm{ramification}(\tau) = \#\,\mathrm{Stab}_{\Gamma_H(M) \cdot \{\pm 1\}}(\tau),$$ the stabiliser being taken inside the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by $\Gamma_H(M)$ together with the integral powers of $-1$.
--
--   The statement identifies the analytic ramification integers of the dictionary with the ramification indices of the quotient map $\mathcal{H} \to X_H(M)$, so that orders of vanishing of modular functions at points of $\mathcal{H}$ translate into multiplicities of divisors on the modular curve; equivalently, $\mathrm{ramification}(\tau)$ is the order of the image of $\mathrm{Stab}_{\Gamma_H(M)}(\tau)$ in $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. It is used in the residue-sum and Abel–Jacobi statements for $\Gamma_H(M)$, and in the computation of the multiplier of a principal divisor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf_two_mul_ramification_eq_card_stabilizer_gammaH.lean

